From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] elfutils: SFrame support, LTO warning hygiene, latent-UB
 hardening, and fix -O0 VLA stack-usage build failure

Consolidated elfutils/libelf patch set (v2).

  A. SFrame support (SHT_GNU_SFRAME / PT_GNU_SFRAME) - fixes three elflint
     self-tests when the toolchain's glibc CRT carries .sframe.
  B. Drop a stray C comment from config/known-dwarf.awk.
  C. Fix the LTO + -Werror build break in libcpu: GCC's -Wnull-dereference
     falsely flags the flex-generated scanner at the final LTO link of
     i386_gendis.  Add -Wno-null-dereference to that link (AM_LDFLAGS).
  D. Fix three latent reads of the uninitialised Dwarf_Off dwp_offset in
     libdwP.h (latent UB; also silences -Wmaybe-uninitialized under LTO).
  E. Kill the LTO-link -Wstack-usage noise for the src/ tools: the
     compile-time _no_Wstack_usage exemptions do not reach the final
     LTO link.  Add -Wno-stack-usage to src/AM_LDFLAGS.
  F. NEW (v2): the eu_search_* test tools declared their worker arrays as
     VLAs (pthread_t threads[num_threads]) with num_threads a non-const
     local, so at -O0 GCC reports 'stack usage might be unbounded' and
     elfutils' -Werror turns it into a build error.  Make num_threads an
     enum constant so the arrays are fixed-size at every -O level.

VALIDATION: applies cleanly (fuzz=0) to elfutils 0.195; at -O0 the four
 eu_search_* programs now compile with elfutils' -Werror (previously
 FAILED with -Werror=stack-usage).  Full suite see VALIDATION_REPORT.md.

=====================================================================
